    <statement><p>An angle of <m>\displaystyle \frac{ 5 \pi}{6}</m> radians can be converted to an angle of <fillin characters="5" name="AnSwEr0001"/> degrees.</p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>150</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><alert>  SOLUTION </alert>




In order to change from radians to degrees, we multiply the number of
radians by <m>\frac{180}{\pi}</m>, so we have



<m>\frac{ 5 \pi}{6} \cdot \frac{180}{\pi} = 150^{\circ}</m>





</solution>
